// Showcase game (#611, docs/showcase-plan.md row 6) — the packs wall as a
// real game, on bgfx. A little city street: the `buildings` pack ships the
// skyline (component + prefabs + atlas + ONE exposed query), the `traffic`
// pack ships the cars that drive past and consumes buildings ONLY through
// that exposed surface (`@import("buildings").queries.count`). The scene
// composes both packs by their NAMESPACED names (`buildings__house`,
// `traffic__car_red`) next to game-root sprites from the `city` atlas.
//
// Contrast with the `packs-demo` fixture: that one probes the wall's
// isolation guarantees headlessly; this one is the same conventions
// (docs/packs.md) rendering an actual scene on a real backend.
//
// VERSION PINS: the RUNTIME packages (core/engine/gfx/cli) + the backend
// pin the RELEASED set — this game proves the released runtime path (see
// tile-explorer's note). bgfx is pinned explicitly (the registry default
// 0.6.6 long predates the current backend train). That pin is 0.20.0, not
// 0.13.1: labelle-core 1.32.0 appended `MaterialEffect.pixel_water` and
// every bgfx release before 0.20.0 switches EXHAUSTIVELY over that enum
// with no arm for it. CI clones labelle-core at `main` as a sibling
// checkout and the assembler's monorepo auto-discovery builds that sibling
// INSTEAD of the `.core_version` pin below, so a pre-0.20.0 bgfx failed
// sema there.
//
// The core pin FOLLOWS the backend pin, not the other way round. The
// assembler unifies every package onto `.core_version`, and released bgfx
// 0.20.0 has a HARD core floor of 1.28.0: `src/gfx/types.zig` types a
// struct field as `core.BackendTextureId` (core#328 phase 3, bgfx >=
// 0.15.0), which is analyzed eagerly. So on a STANDALONE checkout — no
// sibling labelle-core, i.e. the documented `labelle build` path — bgfx
// 0.20.0 over the previous core 1.26.0 pin died inside the backend:
//   labelle-bgfx/src/gfx/types.zig:17:38: error: root source file struct
//   'root' has no member named 'BackendTextureId'
// #731 shipped that pairing claiming it "builds against the pinned
// 1.26.0"; CI never saw it because the sibling core at `main` is >= 1.32.0
// AND the bgfx games are generate-only there (labelle-assembler#732). The
// v1.32.0 names bgfx 0.20.0 takes from `backend_contract` (`PixelWaterDraw`,
// `PIXEL_WATER_*`) are NOT a compile floor — they sit behind
// `@hasField(MaterialEffect, "pixel_water")`-gated paths or lazy top-level
// aliases, and 0.20.0 does compile against core 1.28.0 — but the pin is
// 1.32.0 anyway: the core labelle-bgfx 0.20.0 was released against (its
// own build.zig.zon), the one on which its pixel_water effect is reachable
// at all, and the core the curated `labelle init` trio now carries. So this
// game and a fresh scaffold prove ONE pairing (core 1.32.0 / engine 2.12.2
// / gfx 1.30.1), at or above labelle-bgfx's own `examples/bgfx-android`
// pins (core 1.32.0 / engine 2.11.0 / gfx 1.30.0), satisfying every floor
// in build.zig / `src/init_cmd.zig:checkTrioFloors`. Verified STANDALONE
// (scratch LABELLE_HOME, registry tarballs at these exact tags, no sibling
// checkouts): install → generate → full `zig build`, exit 0. The ASSEMBLER
// is `local:../../` (in-tree source, the examples convention). On the
// fully-RELEASED `labelle` path this game builds on assembler 0.94.0 —
// bgfx takes the generic desktop `unifyCoreDiamond` codegen, unaffected by
// the sokol-desktop byte-anchor gap #611 fixes.
.{
    .name = "pack_city",
    .title = "LaBelle — Pack City Showcase",
    .width = 480,
    .height = 270,
    .target_fps = 60,
    .backend = .bgfx,
    .backend_package = .{ .name = "bgfx", .repo = "github.com/labelle-toolkit/labelle-bgfx", .version = "0.20.0" },
    .y_axis = .down,
    .ecs = .zig_ecs,
    .initial_prefab = "main",
    .states = .{"playing"},
    .resources = .{
        .{ .name = "city", .json = "assets/city.json", .texture = "assets/city.png" },
    },
    .layers = .{
        .{ .name = "world", .order = 0, .space = .world },
    },
    .plugins = .{
        .{ .name = "buildings", .repo = "@packs/buildings" },
        .{ .name = "traffic", .repo = "@packs/traffic" },
    },
    .core_version = "1.32.0",
    .engine_version = "2.12.2",
    .gfx_version = "1.30.1",
    .labelle_version = "1.58.0",
    // In-tree assembler (examples convention). Fully-released path: 0.94.0.
    .assembler_version = "local:../../",
}
